8 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River,\nNorthwest San Juan Mountains, San Juan River Basin and Southwest\nSan Juan Mountains.\n\n* WHEN...Through midnight tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nThis also includes the Gold Mountain, Elk and Ferris burn scars as\nwell as areas of steep, susceptible terrain.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Recent heavy rainfall in southwest Colorado has led to already\nsaturated ground. In addition, multiple rounds of showers and\nthunderstorms are expected through this evening producing periods\nof heavy rainfall and potential flash flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-18T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3a34ecbe968db9fd83e7d289a418ebce8c8e46da.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3a34ecbe968db9fd83e7d289a418ebce8c8e46da.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-18T00:02:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 180002 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 602 PM MDT Thu Sep 17 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Heavy rainfall could result in flash flooding and debris flows through late Friday. A few stronger storms may be capable of producing hail and damaging wind as well. - Flood Watches remain in effect for SE Utah and SW Colorado through this evening. - Cover","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-17T19:22:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION..